  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The three-round granny square works the same corner structure as the four-round version but stops one round earlier, giving a compact 7 cm motif in DK cotton on a 4 mm hook. At this size the square is a useful building block for fine-gauge blankets, bunting, and small accessories where a 10 cm motif would be oversized."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 1 sets four corner spaces with twelve trebles into the magic ring. Round 2 adds a second cluster pair at each corner with a chain-1 space between them. Round 3 fills in the side spaces and finishes with the border round ready for joining."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "tone": "tip",
          "title": "Materials for one motif",
          "body": "About 3 g of DK-weight cotton in one to three colours. A 4 mm crochet hook (UK 8, US G/6). Tapestry needle. Scissors. A blocking mat and pins if you plan to block."
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Gauge" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Each finished three-round granny square measures 7 × 7 cm in DK-weight cotton with a 4 mm hook, after a light steam-block. Work one test motif before starting a large project — a 5% tension difference across 100 squares compounds noticeably."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Stitches used" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "chain (ch) — UK and US shared." }] }] },
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "slip stitch (sl st) — UK and US shared." }] }] },
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "treble (tr) — UK; the same move as US \"double crochet\"." }] }] },
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "magic ring (MR) — adjustable starting loop; no centre hole." }] }] }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Pattern" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Worked in the round, right side facing throughout. Ch 3 at the start of each round counts as the first treble of the first "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [{ "type": "glossaryTooltip", "attrs": { "termSlug": "cluster" } }],
            "text": "cluster"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Do not turn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 1" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Form a magic ring. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). Work 2 tr into the ring. *Ch 2, 3 tr into the ring*; repeat from * to * twice more. Ch 2, sl st to top of beg ch-3 to join. Pull tail to close ring. (12 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 2" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st across next 2 tr and into first "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [{ "type": "glossaryTooltip", "attrs": { "termSlug": "chain-space" } }],
            "text": "chain-space"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Ch 3 (counts as first tr). Into same ch-2 corner sp, work 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr. *Ch 1, into next ch-2 corner sp work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr)*; repeat from * to * twice more. Ch 1, sl st to top of beg ch-3 to join. (24 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces, 4 ch-1 side spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 3" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st across next 2 tr and into first ch-2 corner sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). Into same ch-2 corner sp, work 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr. Ch 1. *Into next ch-1 side sp, work 3 tr. Ch 1. Into next ch-2 corner sp, work (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr). Ch 1.* Repeat from * to * twice more. Into next ch-1 side sp, work 3 tr. Ch 1. Sl st to top of beg ch-3 to join. (36 tr, 4 ch-2 corner spaces, 8 ch-1 side spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Chart" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The chart reads outward from the magic ring, anti-clockwise. Corner chain-2 spaces mark the four corners; chain-1 spaces appear between clusters along the sides from round 2 onward."
          }
        ]
      },
