      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Finishing" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fasten off, leaving a 15 cm tail. Thread the tail through a tapestry needle and weave through 3 to 4 stitches along the back of round 3, then back through 2 to 3 stitches in the opposite direction. Trim. Weave in the magic ring tail along the back of round 1 the same way. Steam-block by holding a steam iron 2 to 3 cm above the motif for 10 seconds, then leave flat to cool."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Joining" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The three-round square joins at its corner ch-2 spaces and its side ch-1 spaces. For a blanket grid, whip-stitch through the back loops with a tapestry needle, or use the join-as-you-go method on the final round of each subsequent square. At 7 cm per square, a 10 x 14 grid gives a 70 x 98 cm lap blanket."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Care" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Handwash in cool water with a small amount of mild soap, or machine-wash on a wool cycle. Do not tumble-dry. Lay flat on a clean towel and ease to shape while damp."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "What to try next" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Once the three-round square is reliable, work the five-round version for a 13 cm motif suitable for cushion covers. The two-colour version changes yarn at the start of round 2 to give a contrasting border round."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
